  "notes": "From the pool-court views (a long pool between the two-storey main house and the yellow guest block; the main house glazed full width on the ground floor under a grey concrete band, yellow upper storey with tall narrow windows; the guest block's yellow face with one horizontal window and one slit; a floating stone stair on the white end wall climbing to the guest block's roof, which carries a sunken yellow lounge under a steel-framed concrete canopy; palms and sunbeds on gravel beside it; tall white party walls). Orientation guessed: street to the south, rear garden to the north. The street front, the rear garden and the exact lot dimensions were not shown and are guessed from a typical narrow Yucatecan lot. Izamal yellow drawn with ochre, the closest material."
